│ to obtain more detailed information about the system.                        │
│ - **Raw data files**: If you want to use the npz data to analyze the system, │
│ you MUST use the `data_analysis_expert` agent to analyze the data. You can   │
│ not analyze the npz data directly.                                           │
│                                                                              │
│ ### NPZ Data Format (for reference - use via `data_analysis_expert` agent)   │
│ Each NPZ file contains:                                                      │
│ - `state`: numpy array, shape `(num_variables, num_steps)` - state           │
│ trajectories                                                                 │
│   - Access: `x1 = data['state'\][0, :\]`, `x2 = data['state'\][1, :\]`       │
│ - `input`: numpy array, shape `(num_inputs, num_steps)` - input signals (if  │
│ applicable)                                                                  │
│   - Access: `u1 = data['input'\][0, :\]`                                     │
│                                                                              │
│ **WARNING**: Do NOT use placeholder names like `<npz_0>` as file paths! Use  │
│ the `data_analysis_expert` agent which has access to the actual file paths.  │
